# Copy to windows/win11.conf and edit. The real file is gitignored.

# Source ISO. Any Windows 11 ISO with sources/install.wim works.
ISO="$HOME/Downloads/Win11_25H2_EnglishInternational_x64_v2.iso"

# Edition to apply. Run `make list-editions` to see what your ISO contains.
# Native VHD boot is a Pro/Enterprise/Education feature - Home is not licensed
# for it.
EDITION="Windows 11 Pro"

# Virtual size of the dynamic VHDX. It only consumes what Windows actually
# uses, but Windows believes it has this much: do not set it far above the free
# space on the stick, or a full stick corrupts the image.
SIZE="48G"

# VHDX payload block size. Left to qemu's auto-calculation this becomes 16 MiB
# for a 48G image, and every scattered NTFS write then claims a whole 16 MiB
# block: a ~14 GiB install produced a 42 GiB file. At 1M the same content is
# ~17 GiB. The stick pays the full file size, so this is the setting that
# decides how much of the stick the image eats.
BLOCK_SIZE="1M"

# Local account created by unattend.xml. Set USERNAME to skip the prompt;
# leave it unset and windows/build.sh asks for the name at the start of the
# build, defaulting to your host account. The password is never stored here -
# build.sh prompts for it on the host and passes it to the container on stdin,
# so it never lands in a file or an environment variable.
#USERNAME="me"
COMPUTERNAME="WIN11-USB"

# en-GB matches the EnglishInternational ISO.
LOCALE="en-GB"
INPUTLOCALE="en-GB"
TIMEZONE="GMT Standard Time"

# Vendor driver packages to put in the image's driver store at build time.
# Windows' inbox set has no driver for any modern GPU, so without this the
# image boots on the Microsoft Basic Display Adapter: odd resolution on the
# laptop panel, and no external monitor. Anything with a .inf under here is
# injected; see windows/drivers/README.md for how to get packages out of a
# vendor download. Leave it unset to use windows/drivers/ when it has
# something in it and build without drivers when it does not.
#DRIVERS_DIR="windows/drivers"

# Where the finished VHDX lands on the stick, relative to the Ventoy partition.
DEST_DIR="/ventoy"
